<header class="site-header"></header>
<main>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap page-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">YZH Dental Lab Workflow</p>
        <h1>One clear path from submitted files to final delivery.</h1>
        <p class="lead">A predictable workflow helps overseas partner labs and clinics test one case, confirm communication and understand how technical decisions are handled before production.</p>
        <div class="cta-row"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/submit-case">Submit a Case</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/services/design-only">View Design Only</a></div>
      </div>
      <img src="/assets/real/full-arch-cad-design-05.jpg" alt="Digital CAD workflow review at YZH Dental Lab" width="1600" height="900" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high">
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Case Path</p>
        <h2>Six steps that keep the case moving.</h2>
        <p class="copy">Each step is designed to reduce guessing, confirm missing details early and keep the technical discussion tied to the case records.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="steps informational-steps">
        <a class="workflow-step" href="/submit-case"><span>01</span><h3>Submit Files</h3><p>Send STL, PLY, ZIP, PDF, photos and the restoration request through the case form.</p></a>
        <a class="workflow-step" href="/services/implant#implant-case-information"><span>02</span><h3>Technical Review</h3><p>Implant system, platform, scanbody, bite, restorative space and material needs are checked.</p></a>
        <a class="workflow-step" href="/submit-case"><span>03</span><h3>Workflow Confirmation</h3><p>We confirm whether the case is design-only, design plus manufacturing, or production support.</p></a>
        <a class="workflow-step" href="/services/digital-workflow"><span>04</span><h3>CAD / Production</h3><p>CAD design, approval communication and approved manufacturing steps move forward.</p></a>
        <a class="workflow-step" href="/about#quality"><span>05</span><h3>Quality Control</h3><p>Fit, contacts, occlusion, finish, components and case notes are checked before release.</p></a>
        <a class="workflow-step" href="/submit-case"><span>06</span><h3>Delivery</h3><p>The finished case is prepared for delivery after the final technical review.</p></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section soft">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Before Production</p>
        <h2>We ask before guessing.</h2>
        <p class="copy">For implant and full-arch work, missing component information can create costly mistakes. The workflow is built to confirm key details before CAD or production continues.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="proof-list">
        <article><h3>Records</h3><p>Scans, bite, photos, prescription and due date are reviewed together.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Implant information</h3><p>Brand, system, platform, scanbody, MUA or Ti-base details are confirmed when relevant.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Design scope</h3><p>Design-only and design-plus-manufacturing cases are handled with different approval needs.</p></article>
        <article><h3>QC handoff</h3><p>Production requirements and quality-control notes stay attached to the case.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section trial">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Start With One Trial Case</p><h2>Send files for technical review.</h2><p class="copy">Use one real case to confirm communication, file quality and the right production path before sending more work.</p></div>
      <div class="cta-panel"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="/submit-case">Submit Case for Review</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/cases">View Case Portfolio</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
